    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bracketed\n\n### Description\n\nI tried to check other issues and I believe this request wasn't ask before, but let me know otherwise.\n\nSince I don't have a US keyboard, my `[`/`]` keys are not \"easy\" to reach, for that reason would be awesome to be able to specify what are the previous/next characters for this plugin (probably the name of the plugin may need to change 😅 ).\n\nI have copy the plugin to my (experimental) config and did a couple of changes to see how it would work (if you want, I can create a PR). The changes needed would be these 3:\n```lua\nMiniBracketed.config = {\n  previous   = \"[\",\n  next       = \"]\",\n```\n\n```lua\nH.setup_config = function(config)\n  ...\n  H.check_type('previous', config.previous, 'string')\n  H.check_type('next', config.next, 'string')\n```\n\nand in every map\n```lua\n    H.map(..., config.previous .. up, ...)\n    H.map(..., config.next .. up, ...)\n    H.map(..., config.previous .. low, ...)\n    H.map(..., config.next .. low, ...)\n```\n\nand obviously, fix documentation, plugin name, and linking to the plugin\n\nPS: the name of the plugin could be `previousnext` similar to the `splitjoin`",
