            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI don't think this is a good idea to have in 'mini.bracketed'. Using `[` and `]` keys aligns with built-in Vim mappings and is a long-standing convention to use as \"previous\" and \"next\". And renaming module is obviously asking too much.\n\nHere are alternatives to consider here:\n- Remap `[` and `]` keys to something more suitable for the keyboard layout. Here is [an example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/235#issuecomment-1462367177): basically just having `nmap <key1> [` and `nmap <key2> ]` should work here (notice the usage of `remap = true`). And then use `<key1>b` and `<key2>b` as if `[b` and `]b`.\n- [Create custom mappings from scratch](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/8f0969dd976e4f0cb8e2898596fa2eab18ce676b/doc/mini-bracketed.txt#L175-L184) (although that would require disabling all of them and creating many mappings in several modes).\n\nClosing as not planned.",
